{"id":"sigmoid_kernel","title":"Sigmoid similarity transform","family":"kernel","definition":"reference","intro_en":"This sigmoid score maps an affine inner product through tanh. The animation shows saturation: sufficiently large input scores compress into a narrow output range. The formula is commonly called a sigmoid kernel, but arbitrary scale and offset choices do not guarantee a positive-semidefinite Gram matrix.","intro_zh":"该 sigmoid 分数将内积的仿射变换送入 tanh。动图展示饱和现象：较大输入分数被压缩到很窄的输出范围。该公式常称为 sigmoid 核，但任意尺度与偏置选择不保证 Gram 矩阵半正定。","steps_en":["Use the same aligned coordinate system for both vectors.","Compute and sum the coordinatewise contributions shown in the plot.","Apply the specified scalar kernel transformation to that complete sum.","Read the pair score; kernel magnitude is not a calibrated similarity probability."],"steps_zh":["对两个向量使用同一个已对齐坐标系。","计算图示逐坐标贡献并求和。","对完整求和结果施加指定的标量核变换。","读取成对分数；核函数量级不是校准后的相似概率。"],"formula":"K(x,y)=tanh(0.1*dot(x,y)-0.5)","caveats_en":["A bounded output does not establish positive semidefiniteness or a probabilistic interpretation; saturation can hide changes in the input dot product.","No local time warping is performed by this aligned-vector construction."],"caveats_zh":["输出有界不能证明半正定性或概率解释；饱和可能掩盖输入内积变化。","此已对齐向量构造不执行局部时间扭曲。"],"sources":[{"label":"scikit-learn: pairwise kernels and their formulas","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/metrics.html"}],"x":[0.2,0.4,1.1,2.4,3.2,2.5,1.2,0.3,-0.4,-0.1],"y":[0.1,0.3,0.5,1.2,2.6,3.1,2.3,1.1,0.2,-0.3],"input_label":"Deterministic illustrative arrays; no benchmark data","parameters":{"preprocessing":"none","gamma":0.1,"coef0":-0.5},"result":{"label":"kernel score","value":0.9433898073781448,"detail":"The explicit definition and parameters shown on this card."},"frames":[{"phase":0,"caption":"Compute the indicated contribution at each aligned index","panel":{"kind":"bars","title":"Coordinate products","a":[0.020000000000000004,0.12],"labels":["1","2"],"marker":1,"a_label":"contribu